# ORCHESTRA · FIELD CLOCK played by jellies: every sound is a stimulus to a nerve, and a nerve may refuse
@prompt the field clock keeps time, and the jellies keep it with their bodies
@world lab song=a4-clock until=40s
@cast kick:sentinel role=kick
@cast snare:celluloid role=snare
@cast hat:doodle role=hat
@cast bass:mantle role=bass
@cast choir:glass role=choir
@camera orbit dist=11 speed=0.8
@light "Music Box 1:n"
@ekphrasis 0s..6s "each jelly is cast to one sound; its onsets fire that jelly's pacemaker"
@ekphrasis 20s..26s "a refused onset is the refractory nerve, not a bug"
@test 20s beats kick >= 4
@test 40s fired kick >= 0.3
@test 40s visible choir
